metamusic worker image - third-party notices

This image contains the YuE2 VAE weights, baked in at build time so that the endpoint needs only one cached
model (the 3B model, which is NOT in the image):

  Model:     YuE2-Vae
  Source:    https://huggingface.co/m-a-p/YuE2-Vae  (pinned revision: see VAE_REVISION in worker/Dockerfile)
  Creators:  multimodal-art-projection (m-a-p) and the YuE2 licensors
  Licence:   Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0)
             https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
             with the individual-creator permission and the academic-use terms of the YuE2 MODEL_LICENSE
             https://github.com/multimodal-art-projection/YuE/blob/main/MODEL_LICENSE
  Changes:   none (files are verified byte-for-byte against the SHA-256 listed by Hugging Face)

The weights are used for non-commercial, individual creative use under those terms. The licence text,
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the licenses/ directory of the model repository are kept next to the weights in
/opt/mm/hf-cache/hub/models--m-a-p--YuE2-Vae/snapshots/<revision>/.

The image also installs the yue2 inference code (multimodal-art-projection/YuE, pinned commit in
worker/contract/YUE2_COMMIT, Apache-2.0) and Python packages under their own licences (see
/opt/venv/freeze.txt for the list).

Tier B listening check ("ears"). The image also bakes in three models for the post-render analysis stage, each at a pinned
revision and verified byte-for-byte against the SHA-256 in worker/ears/models.lock.json (/opt/mm/ears-models.lock.json in the image);
none is modified and each is MIT-licensed (licence texts: /opt/mm/licenses/ears/):

  Model:     htdemucs (Hybrid Transformer Demucs, vocal separation)
  Source:    https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/demucs/hybrid_transformer/955717e8-8726e21a.th  (Demucs, Meta Platforms)
  Licence:   MIT (demucs-LICENSE-MIT.txt)

  Model:     faster-whisper-large-v3 (Whisper large-v3 converted for CTranslate2, speech recognition)
  Source:    https://huggingface.co/Systran/faster-whisper-large-v3  (pinned revision in the lock)
  Creators:  OpenAI (Whisper), SYSTRAN (conversion)
  Licence:   MIT (whisper-LICENSE-MIT.txt, faster-whisper-LICENSE-MIT.txt)

  Model:     torchcrepe "full" (CREPE pitch tracking weights as packaged by torchcrepe)
  Source:    https://github.com/maxrmorrison/torchcrepe  (pinned commit in the lock)
  Licence:   MIT (torchcrepe-LICENSE-MIT.txt)

The libraries that run them (demucs, julius, faster-whisper, ctranslate2, torchcrepe and their dependencies) are installed from PyPI
under /opt/ears-site at hash-pinned versions (worker/requirements-ears.txt) and keep their own licences (MIT, BSD, ISC, Apache-2.0).
Two of them are LGPL and are used unmodified, as ordinary importable packages that a user may replace: lameenc (LGPL-3.0-or-later,
a Demucs dependency this image never calls) and soxr (LGPL-2.1-or-later, a librosa dependency). ctranslate2 loads the NVIDIA cuBLAS
and cuDNN runtime libraries that torch's CUDA wheels already ship in /opt/venv. The CTranslate2 licence is ctranslate2-LICENSE-MIT.txt.
